From 682b98c54dde5e0ed709b2c4a505b915e223bbea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 13:23:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 064/109] rust: drm: kms: add typed color and rotation
 properties

Add typed KMS property support for CRTC colour management and plane
rotation.

ColorLut exposes validated drm_color_lut entries without generated
bindings, and ColorCtm exposes a colour transformation matrix.
enable_color_mgmt() creates the DEGAMMA_LUT, CTM and GAMMA_LUT
properties, with enable_gamma() as the gamma-only shorthand, and the
CRTC state accessors read back what userspace programmed.

Decode the CTM here rather than in each driver: its UAPI entries are
S31.32 sign-magnitude rather than two's complement, so reading them as
signed integers turns every negative coefficient into a large positive
one and a darkening correction saturates instead.

Rotation represents only combinations accepted by the DRM rotation
property, while the plane state accessors expose placement and
cursor-hotspot coordinates needed by software and transport scanout
drivers.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-0
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
